# N=10 traversals — empirical validation of the linear-extrapolation
# mission-scaling claim.
#
# A "traversal" here = one 5-step single-direction crawl. 5 forward +
# 5 reverse = 10 traversals = 50 steps total. The robot returns to its
# initial pose at (2a, 2b) after every two traversals (one cycle).
#
# Acceptance criteria:
#   - All 50 docks succeed (d < 5 mm AND ori < 5°).
#   - Per-dock structure attitude stays bounded (no monotonic growth
#     across cycles → confirms sign-symmetry).
#   - After 120s trailing settle, irreversible θ_s residual scales
#     sub-linearly with N (random walk √N or better, not 10× linear).
#   - ‖h_w‖ at settle end stays ~one-traversal-scale (~0.13 Nms), not
#     N× = ~1.3 Nms.

START anchor_3a anchor_3b

# === Cycle 1 (traversals 1 & 2) ===
# Forward
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_5a
DOCK anchor_6b
# Reverse
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_3a
DOCK anchor_3b

# === Cycle 2 (traversals 3 & 4) ===
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_5a
DOCK anchor_6b
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_3a
DOCK anchor_3b

# === Cycle 3 (traversals 5 & 6) ===
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_5a
DOCK anchor_6b
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_3a
DOCK anchor_3b

# === Cycle 4 (traversals 7 & 8) ===
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_5a
DOCK anchor_6b
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_3a
DOCK anchor_3b

# === Cycle 5 (traversals 9 & 10) ===
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_5a
DOCK anchor_6b
DOCK anchor_5b
DOCK anchor_4a
DOCK anchor_4b
DOCK anchor_3a
DOCK anchor_3b
